course: dictionary
lesson: 15896
title: Undone words and clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts. Look at «unlaced». The start, un-, often means undo or not, and lace is the string that holds a shoe closed. So unlaced means the laces have been undone. «Mia's trainers were unlaced, so she tripped on the stairs.» Trainers that are undone can come loose and make you trip.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «Mia's trainers were with the laces undone, so she tripped on the stairs.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Unlace can also be a verb, an action word. «Sam unlaced his boots and sat down.» Here unlace means to undo the laces. The past form, unlaced, tells us the action has already happened.
fact: Unlaced means with the laces undone or taken out.
fact: As a verb, to unlace something means to undo its laces.
fact: Unlace, unlaces, unlaced and unlacing all come from the same verb.
fact: «Unlaced» is the past form of «unlace».
fact: The prefix un- often means undo or not, as in «unlaced», «unlock» and «unfold».
exercise: «Mia's trainers were unlaced, so she tripped on the stairs.» What does unlaced mean? | Tied in a tight bow | Clean and shiny | *With the laces undone | Very new
exercise: To unlace something means what? | To wash it | *To undo its laces | To make it wet | To tie a knot
exercise: After a long march, why might soldiers unlace their boots? | *To give their feet some room and relief | To add more laces | To tie them tighter | To make their boots shine
test: «Sam unlaced his trainers and kicked them off.» What does unlaced mean here? | Had lost a sole | Had been painted | *Had the laces undone | Had been cleaned with water
test: Which word is the past form of unlace? | *unlaced | unlacing | unlaces | unlace
exam: «Before the race, Ben checked that his laces were not unlaced.» What does this tell us? | Ben's laces had been undone | *Ben's laces were still tied | Ben had no laces at all | Ben had lost his race
